{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Et HaShem you have declared.</b> You have designated — for HaShem, blessed be He, agreed to be for you an Elohim, through your accepting His commandments upon yourself, and He likewise. <b>He has declared you.</b> He has moved you — that you said you would be to Him a treasured people, because He performed for you signs and mighty deeds." "<b>You have declared.</b> In the vernacular, you have affirmed. Another interpretation: the language of exchange — you exchanged all fears in the world for Him, for you set them all aside and chose Him; and likewise He exchanged all the ancient nations and chose you, to keep His commandments. And the alef is a root radical that drops, like the alef of אזרוע, of אסוך, of אתמול. Another interpretation: the language of praise, as in 'let all workers of iniquity be praised' — no, as in יתאמרו כל פועלי און."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The Old French gloss 'פאישדיר״ה' is rendered 'you have affirmed' based on the expected Old French 'vous avés dit' or similar; exact vocalization uncertain. The last clause appears corrupt in the Hebrew: the verse cited (Ps. 92:8, 'יתאמרו כל פועלי און') means 'shall flourish,' and the contradictory negative gloss 'no' may reflect a scribal or transcriptional difficulty. Transmitted hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:26.372479965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}